{"name":"Hummus","hex":"#eecc99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hummus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Levantine Arab dip made of chickpea paste with various additions, such as olive oil, fresh garlic, lemon juice, and tahini, often eaten with pitta bread, or as a meze."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hummus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hummus","blocks":[{"text":"Hummus is a Levantine dip, spread, or savory dish made from cooked, mashed chickpeas blended with tahini, lemon juice, and garlic. The standard garnish includes olive oil, a few whole chickpeas, parsley, and paprika."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Lebanese_style_hummus.jpg/330px-Lebanese_style_hummus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hummus","wikidata":"Q241987"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/Hummuswithpinenuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/Hummuswithpinenuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Hummus with pine nuts and olive oil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHummuswithpinenuts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Houmous.jpg/500px-Houmous.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Houmous.jpg/1280px-Houmous.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Houmous.jpg/500px-Houmous.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hummus served in a bowl on a platter of pita bread","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHoumous.jpg"}],"sounds":{"hummus":[{"ty